 " files with the statistics"
}], "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7800336783762503`*^9, 3.7800336946692457`*^9}, {
  3.780034213957883*^9, 3.780034214578864*^9}, {3.7878135971320333`*^9, 
  3.787813605392315*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"94babd65-8244-4d8b-b0a4-\
b6b7a18a9bfe"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["These are the quantities/coefficients that are fitted \
accross parameter space for the amplitude. \n\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Int1\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Int2\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
are the two collocation points in the intermediate region.\n\
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Int0\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]DInt0\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] are the value and \
derivative at the extra collocation point that we use when splitting in two \
intermediate regions for the EMR cases.\n\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]ALambda\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Lambda\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Sigma\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] are the coefficients of \
the ringdown ansatz.\n\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Insp1\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Insp2\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Insp3\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] are the collocation \
points for the inspiral. ",
 FontColor->GrayLevel[0]]], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7877244763637257`*^9, 3.787724522089306*^9}, 
   3.787725279063814*^9, {3.787725322282666*^9, 3.787725369248917*^9}, {
   3.787725481609785*^9, 
   3.787725604880144*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"50411e2d-4a86-418e-b826-\
9c71492d2af4"],

