Cell["\<\
For each mode and each quantity we generate latex files that includes a table \
with all the values, absolute and relative errors of all the coefficients of \
the fits.  
This is done by the function \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]TeXTableOneCoefficient\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] that reads a .m file that contains all the info \
needed for one coefficient.
This function also  returns the functional of the fit. E.g. for exampe, \
Fits21 contains the fits of all the quantities listed in \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]listOfquantities21\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote].\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7877245298353863`*^9, 3.787724537853993*^9}, {
  3.7877245910583467`*^9, 3.7877247160115967`*^9}, {3.787725707131557*^9, 
  3.787725779200038*^9}, {3.787814458374386*^9, 
  3.787814609051427*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"03bbf0a6-029a-4643-a103-\
b8ea52259aa7"],

